{{See also|Free-to-play transportation}}
[[File:Transportation logo.png|right|150px]]
'''Transportation''' includes all of the varied means of getting around the world of ''[[Old School RuneScape]]''.

==Efficient transportation==
To get around in an efficient manner, you should consider the following things:
*Train your [[Agility]] for faster restoration of [[run energy]].
*Use [[weight-reducing gear]] to run for longer periods.
*Train your [[Magic]] level to unlock [[teleport spells]], or purchase [[teleport tablets]] instead.
*Complete quests to gain access to transportation methods such as [[spirit tree]]s, [[fairy ring]]s, [[gnome glider]]s and certain spells.
*By training up your [[Construction]] you can add various transportation methods to your [[Player owned house|house]] such as [[Jewellery_box_space|jewellery boxes]], portals with teleports from all spellbooks, and mounted amulets. Your house can eventually serve as a hub for transportation around the map which you can access using only [[house teleports]].
**If you do not have all of the useful transportation options in your house, consider joining world 330 if your [[POH|house]] is in [[Rimmington]], to use the facilities of houses of high level hosts if available. Join their house using the [[House Advertisement]] facility, and use their installed teleportation methods. If the hosts have maxed out houses, they often also have [[rejuvenation pool]]s, restoring your run energy. Especially for low-level players, this method opens up an extreme range of teleportation options for the price of just one house teleport.
*To reach useful locations like banks, skilling resources and facilities or other transport network nodes, familiarize yourself with the [[Closest...|closest]] transportation destinations to various useful features.

==Foot travel==
{{See also|Energy|Run trick}}
Walking or running is the basic method of travel. The amount of weight carried determines how long a player can run, while  their [[Agility]] level impacts their run energy restoration rate. The more weight you carry, the shorter distance you can run. Additionally, pressing the Control key and clicking on a part of the map temporarily turns on run.

* '''Agility shortcuts and obstacles:'''  By taking shortcuts, a player is able to reach a destination faster. The higher the [[Agility]] level, the more shortcuts are available. There are also obstacles, which are similar to shortcuts, but have one major difference: using these agility obstacles is the only way to get to that certain area.

==Teleportation==
[[File:Teleport.gif|thumb|right|A player teleporting]]
Teleportation is the instant travel from any location to a specific location elsewhere. This can take a number of different forms.

